# Clause-alt proposals for the Wine, Beer & Spirits overviews (6 Nov 2026). Facts come only from the Gemini overview; the alt reorders and splits.
R='range'; L='lump'; M='mixed'
ALT={
'algarve':("The Algarve DOC covers subregions like Lagoa and Tavira, where estates pour blends featuring the native Negra Mole grape. Inland, the Monchique mountains are the center for aguardente de medronho, a strong brandy distilled from local strawberry tree fruit.","Opens with a range sentence (wines and spirits), then wine, then spirit. Now wine first, the brandy at the end."),
'amalfi':("The Amalfi Coast is known for its terraced vineyards producing Costa d'Amalfi DOC wines. Visitors can tour steep, cliffside estates in subzones like Furore, Ravello, and Tramonti, and the grape harvest in early fall provides the most active vineyard experience. The coast's signature liqueur is limoncello, and small workshops let visitors taste spirits made from local sfusato amalfitano lemons.","Range opener, then wine and spirit mixed in the visit sentence. Now wine (with its harvest) first, limoncello at the end."),
'amsterdam':("Amsterdam's historic proeflokalen (tasting houses) in the city center serve local jenever (Dutch gin). A modern craft beer scene follows, with independent breweries in former industrial spaces and seasonal bock beers in autumn.","Opens with a mixed range sentence, then one sentence covering jenever and beer together. Now jenever, then beer."),
'argentine-lake-district':("The Argentine Lake District is known for its craft beer scene, centered in Bariloche, where visitors can tour breweries and taste local IPAs and stouts. Its cool-climate wines come from the Río Negro and Neuquén valleys, with wineries producing Pinot Noir and Merlot. The warmer months are best for outdoor beer gardens and vineyard visits.","Range opener, then breweries and wineries share one sentence. Now beer first, wine second."),
'aspen':("Aspen's biggest drinks event is the massive Food & Wine Classic in June, which draws producers and sommeliers to the mountains. Visitors can taste local potato vodka at nearby distilleries in Basalt, or drink local ales in downtown taprooms.","Range opener, then the event comes last. I led with the Food & Wine Classic as the clearest draw; swap if you disagree."),
'atacama':("The Atacama's most distinctive wines come from oasis villages like Toconao, where grapes grow at elevations over 8,000 feet, and visitors can taste them there. Local bars also infuse Chilean pisco with native desert herbs like rica-rica and muña-muña.","Range opener (wine and botanical spirits), then wine, then spirit. Now wine first, pisco at the end."),
'athens':("Athens is a center for Greek wine. Visitors can taste indigenous grape varieties like Assyrtiko and Xinomavro at wine bars in the city center, or visit wineries in the nearby Attica region, known for Savatiano. Traditional spirits like ouzo, tsipouro, and mastiha are widely available. A growing craft beer scene rounds it out, with local breweries producing modern craft beers.","Range opener, and the last sentence lumps spirits and beer together with 'while'. Now wine, then spirits, then beer."),
'azores':("The Azores produce distinct volcanic wines, most notably on Pico Island where vines grow inside stone walls called currais. Visitors can tour these UNESCO-recognized vineyards, taste crisp whites made from Arinto dos Açores and Verdelho grapes, or visit the Biscoitos wine region on Terceira, with the best vineyard access during the late summer harvest. The islands also produce passionfruit liqueurs and local beers.","The vineyard-access months were lumped onto the end of the liqueur and beer sentence. Moved next to the vineyards."),
'banff':("Banff and Jasper's mountain-town breweries make small-batch ales, and local distilleries produce botanical gins. The scene is driven by local glacier water, and the best time to explore is during the late fall beer festivals or the busy summer patio season.","Range opener ('a craft beverage scene'), then breweries and distilleries in one sentence. Now beer first, gin second."),
'barcelona':("Just outside Barcelona, the Penedès and Alella regions provide easy day trips to taste Cava and crisp white wines directly at the cellars, and the late summer and early autumn grape harvest brings festivals and peak vineyard activity. In the city itself, daytime vermouth is a local tradition, and there is a prominent craft beer scene.","Range opener, then the harvest sentence is tacked on after the Cava sentence. Now Cava and the harvest together first, vermouth and beer at the end. I took Cava as the biggest draw."),
'basque-country':("The Basque Country is known for Txakoli, a slightly sparkling, dry white wine poured from a height. Visitors can tour the coastal vineyards, and the Rioja Alavesa subregion produces robust red wines. Traditional cider (sagardoa) is served in cider houses (sagardotegiak), and the pintxo bars of San Sebastián and Bilbao pair local drinks with small bites.","Wine and cider are interleaved in the first sentence and the visit sentence. Now wine, then cider and the bars."),
'bavaria-munich':("Munich centers on massive beer halls and shaded beer gardens pouring Helles and Weissbier, and Bavaria is defined by its brewing heritage. The scene shifts from outdoor summer drinking under chestnut trees to indoor strong beer festivals in early spring. To the north, Franconia is wine country, producing crisp Silvaner wines bottled in traditional rounded Bocksbeutel, and it specializes in smoked Rauchbier.","Range opener (brewing and wine country), then the season sentence lands after the wine. Now beer and its seasons together, Franconia at the end."),
'beijing':("Beijing's drinking culture is anchored by craft beer, with many breweries tucked into the city's historic hutongs. Traditionalists can try Erguotou, the city's fiery local style of baijiu. The outskirts hold emerging wine regions like Fangshan, and the milder spring and autumn months are the most comfortable for exploring.","The baijiu and wine share one 'while' sentence. Now one topic per sentence."),
'bend-crater-lake':("Bend is a major hub for Pacific Northwest craft beer, anchored by the Bend Ale Trail which connects dozens of local breweries. Visitors drink on sunny outdoor patios in the summer and by fire pits after skiing in the winter. The region also produces high-desert spirits and craft cider.","The patio and fire-pit season sentence sits after the spirits and cider. Now beer and its seasons together, the 'also' at the end."),
'berlin':("Berlin's beer scene runs from sprawling outdoor beer gardens pouring classic pilsners to a modern wave of craft breweries. Visitors can taste Berliner Weisse, a sour wheat beer traditionally mixed with woodruff or raspberry syrup, and the outdoor drinking culture peaks in the warmer months. Local distilleries and historic spirits manufacturers produce Korn and gin, and visitors can tour them.","Range opener (beer gardens to distilleries), then beer and spirits are mixed. Now beer first, spirits at the end."),
'big-island':("The Big Island's small local alcohol scene is built on its tropical climate and volcanic soil. Visitors can tour breweries in Kona and Hilo. Near Volcano, a winery uses local fruits like jaboticaba and guava, and spirits are distilled from local sugarcane and macadamia nuts.","One sentence lists beer, wine and spirits together. Now beer, then the fruit winery and spirits."),
'black-forest':("The Black Forest is bordered by the Baden wine region, known for Spätburgunder and Grauburgunder along the Baden Wine Route, and the harvest season brings new wine and lively festivals to the vineyard terraces. Local distilleries craft Schwarzwälder Kirschwasser and other fruit brandies. Traditional breweries produce regional pilsners and wheat beers.","The harvest sentence was lumped after the breweries and distilleries. Now wine and its harvest together first, brandy then beer at the end."),
'budapest':("Budapest is a hub for Hungarian wine, from Tokaji to Villány reds, and a short trip to the Etyek-Buda wine region brings cellar tastings. The scene peaks in September during the Budapest Wine Festival at Buda Castle. The herbal bitter Unicum is a Hungarian staple, and visitors can tour the Zwack distillery. Craft beer halls in District IX round out the city.","Range opener (Unicum to wines), then spirits, beer and wine in one sentence, then the wine festival. Now wine and its festival first. I led with wine; swap with Unicum if you disagree."),
'buenosaires':("Buenos Aires is a major hub for Argentine wine. While the vineyards are far away, the city's wine bars and tasting rooms pour Malbec from Mendoza, Torrontés from Salta, and Pinot Noir from Patagonia. Craft breweries are concentrated in neighborhoods like Palermo and San Telmo. Local vermouth is a staple of the city's aperitif culture.","Range opener (wine, beer and spirits), then the last sentence mixes beer and vermouth. Now wine, then beer, then vermouth."),
'canaries':("The Canary Islands produce volcanic wines, most notably in Lanzarote's La Geria region and across Tenerife's five appellations. Visitors can tour bodegas to taste crisp Malvasía and earthy Listán Negro, and the late summer harvest and November's new wine festivals provide the most active tasting experiences. Gran Canaria is also known for traditional honey rum.","The honey rum was mixed into the wine visit sentence and the harvest closed the paragraph. Now wine and its harvest together, rum at the end."),
'cape-cod-islands':("Cape Cod and the islands of Nantucket and Martha's Vineyard produce coastal wines, including cranberry wines, tasted at vineyard tasting rooms. Maritime-inspired ales are served at outdoor beer gardens, and locally distilled rum adds to the small-batch spirits. The scene peaks in summer when outdoor spaces open, while fall brings grape and cranberry harvests.","Range opener (wines, beers, spirits), then one long list. Now wine, then beer, then spirits."),
'cape-town':("Cape Town is a major global wine destination, anchored by the historic Constantia Valley within the city and the nearby Cape Winelands. Visitors can tour centuries-old Cape Dutch wine estates and taste local Pinotage and Chenin Blanc, and the late summer harvest brings active cellar tours and regional festivals. Urban craft breweries and gin distilleries in neighborhoods like Woodstock round out the scene.","The harvest sentence was lumped after the breweries and gin. Now the wine and harvest together, breweries and gin at the end."),
'chamonix':("The French Alps feature the high-altitude Savoie wine region, known for crisp white wines like Jacquère and Altesse, alongside red Mondeuse. Visitors can tour vineyard cellar doors in the valleys. Herbal alpine liqueurs like Génépi are tasted in mountain towns, and a strong local craft beer scene thrives around Chamonix.","The cellar-door visit and the liqueur share one 'or' sentence. Now one topic per sentence."),
'charleston-savannah':("Charleston and Savannah's craft beverage scene centers on numerous local breweries, with taprooms pouring regional IPAs, sours, and stouts. Distilleries produce small-batch bourbon, rum, and gin, and a growing number of cideries round out the scene. The region is also known for its historic drinking culture, including Savannah's open-container laws in the historic district.","Range opener (breweries, distilleries, cideries), then spirits and taprooms in one sentence. Now beer, then spirits, then cider."),
'chicago':("Chicago is a major craft beer hub, anchored by neighborhood brewery districts like Ravenswood's Malt Row and the West Loop. Visitors can tour production facilities and drink at expansive beer gardens, and the scene peaks in summer and fall during outdoor street festivals and barrel-aged beer releases. Chicago's local spirits include the notoriously bitter Malört.","The spirit (Malört) was in the middle of the beer visit sentence and the beer season came after it. Now beer and its season together, Malört at the end."),
'chilean-lake-district':("The Chilean Lake District is known for its craft beer scene, rooted in the region's German heritage, and visitors can tour breweries in Valdivia and Puerto Varas. Emerging cool-climate wines, local cider (chicha) and spirits round out the scene. The best time to visit is during the warmer months when beer gardens and vineyard tours are fully accessible.","Range opener (beer and wine), then breweries, cider and spirits share one sentence. Now beer first, the rest at the end."),
'colombian-andes':("The Colombian Andes are known for traditional fermented drinks. Visitors can try chicha, a fermented corn drink, and aguardiente, an anise-flavored spirit, in local taverns and rural towns, where smaller towns feature regional variations. Bogotá and Medellín also have established craft breweries.","Range opener (fermented drinks and craft beer), then the beer sits mid-way. Now the traditional drinks first, the breweries at the end."),
'colombian-caribbean':("The Colombian Caribbean has established rum traditions, with rum tasting rooms in Cartagena. Microbreweries in the Sierra Nevada add a developing craft beer scene, using local ingredients like coffee and coca leaves. Fermented drinks like guarapo are common along the coast.","Range opener (beer and rum), then rum and beer share a sentence. Now rum first, beer and fermented drinks after."),
'copenhagen':("Copenhagen is a major hub for Nordic craft beer, with microbreweries in the Vesterbro and Nørrebro districts, and its brewing culture peaks during spring beer festivals and the release of holiday ales in late fall. Traditional Danish spirits also feature, including house-infused aquavit paired with traditional lunches.","Range opener (beer and spirits), then the beer visit and aquavit share one 'or' sentence. Now beer and its season together, aquavit at the end."),
'cornwall':("Cornwall produces traditional ales and ciders. Visitors can tour historic breweries and sample farm-pressed scrumpy. Cool-climate wines are a growing output, with estates specializing in sparkling wines, and craft gins are also made. The warmer months provide the most reliable access to cellar doors and outdoor tastings.","Range opener (ales, ciders, wines, gins), then beer and wine share a sentence. Now ales and cider, then wine, then gin at the end."),
'cotswolds':("The Cotswolds produces traditional English cask ales. The region's limestone hills support a growing English sparkling wine scene, and summer and early autumn provide the best conditions for vineyard walks. The surrounding Gloucestershire area is known for traditional cider and perry, with cider orchard visits, and the region also produces local single malt whisky and dry gin.","Range opener (ales, whisky, gin), then wine, cider and the season are tangled. Now ale, wine with its season, cider, then spirits at the end."),
'gbr':("The coastal towns serving the reef have a growing tropical craft beer scene, with microbreweries in Cairns and Port Douglas making refreshing ales suited to the heat. Inland day trips to the Atherton Tablelands reveal distilleries turning local sugar cane and tropical fruits into rum and liqueurs.","Range opener (beer and spirits), then breweries. Now beer in one sentence and spirits in the next."),
'hokkaido':("Hokkaido is a major center for Japanese brewing. Visitors can tour the historic brick buildings of the Sapporo Beer Museum, and the scene peaks in summer during the massive outdoor beer festivals in Sapporo. Single malts are tasted at the Nikka Whisky Yoichi Distillery, and the vineyards of the Yoichi and Furano wine regions can be explored.","Range opener (brewing, distilling and winemaking), then beer, whisky and wine in one sentence, with the beer festival last. Now beer and its festival together, then whisky, then wine."),
'hongkong':("Hong Kong has a growing local craft beer scene, with small breweries in industrial areas like Wong Chuk Hang and Kwun Tong. A few urban distilleries make gin infused with regional botanicals. It is not a traditional production region, and the experience is largely indoors.","Range opener (beer and distilleries), then breweries or gin in one 'or' sentence. Now beer, then gin."),
'hudson-valley':("The Hudson Valley has a long history of winemaking, and the Shawangunk Wine Trail and Dutchess Wine Trail connect vineyards. The best time to visit is late summer through fall, when the harvest is in full swing. A booming scene for cider, beer, and spirits includes farm breweries and cideries that use local apples and hops.","Range opener, then the harvest sentence closes after the beer and cider. Now wine and its harvest together, the booming other scene at the end."),
'ireland':("Ireland is famous for its stout, and visitors can explore the Guinness Storehouse in Dublin. The whiskey trail runs through the Midlands and Cork, with historic distilleries open for tours and tastings. Craft beers and ciders are sampled in local pubs, and summer brings more outdoor festivals and longer hours at rural distilleries.","Range opener (stout and whiskey), then the visit sentence mixes the Storehouse, whiskey and craft beer. Now stout, then whiskey, then craft beer and cider."),
'istanbul':("Istanbul's drinking culture centers on meyhanes, traditional taverns where locals pair rakı, an anise-flavored spirit, with meze. The city also features wine bars pouring Turkish varietals like Öküzgözü and Kalecik Karası from Thrace and Anatolia. A growing craft beer presence is found in neighborhoods like Kadıköy and Bomonti.","Wine bars and craft beer share the last sentence. Split so each gets its own."),
'lisbon':("Lisbon is a gateway to Portuguese viticulture, surrounded by historic wine regions like Colares and Bucelas, and the harvest season in early fall brings the most activity to nearby vineyards. In the historic center, visitors can taste Ginjinha, the city's traditional sour cherry liqueur. The Marvila district has a concentration of craft breweries.","The harvest sentence was lumped after the breweries and Ginjinha. Now wine and its harvest together, the liqueur and breweries at the end."),
'london':("London is a historic center for cask ale, with a modern craft brewing scene concentrated in railway arches, and visitors can walk the Bermondsey Beer Mile. Traditional gin is also a London staple, with urban distilleries that can be toured. Day trips reach the English sparkling wine vineyards in nearby Kent and Sussex, and the warmer months are best for vineyard tours and outdoor brewery taprooms.","Range opener (ale and gin), then gin, beer and wine share the visit sentence. Now ale, then gin, then wine."),
'los-cabos':("Los Cabos has a growing craft beer scene, with local breweries in San José del Cabo and Cabo San Lucas. Regional Baja wines can be sampled in dedicated tasting rooms, and Damiana, a traditional herbal liqueur native to the peninsula, is also served.","Range opener (beer and spirits), then beer, wine and liqueur in one list. Now beer, then wine, then the liqueur."),
'mallorca':("Mallorca produces distinct local wines, particularly from the indigenous Manto Negro and Callet grapes. The Binissalem and Pla i Llevant regions hold the main wineries, many of which host tastings and tours, and the harvest season brings wine festivals to the island's interior. A growing craft beer scene and traditional spirits like Hierbas round out the island's drinks.","Beer and spirits were in the first sentence with the wine, and the harvest closed the paragraph. Now wine and its harvest together, beer and spirits at the end."),
'marlborough-abel-tasman':("Marlborough produces most of New Zealand's wine, with dozens of cellar doors pouring its signature Sauvignon Blanc, and visitors can bike between vineyards in the Wairau Valley. Next door, the Nelson region grows the country's hops, supporting a dense trail of craft breweries and cider makers, and visitors can tour hop farms and taprooms around Nelson.","The last sentence mixes the vineyards and hop farms. Now wine with its biking, then beer with its tours."),
'maui':("Maui's alcohol scene relies on tropical agriculture, with spirits distilled from local sugar cane. Wines fermented from pineapples are made too, and visitors can tour production facilities in Upcountry Maui and Kihei. The island also supports a major craft brewing industry that distributes across the Pacific.","Range opener (spirits and wines), then one visit sentence. Now spirits, then wine with the tours, then beer at the end."),
'mexicocity':("Mexico City is a major hub for tasting traditional Mexican spirits. Visitors can visit dedicated tasting rooms in Roma and Condesa for artisanal mezcal, sotol, and tequila sourced from across the country, and historic pulquerías pour fermented agave sap. A growing craft beer movement features taprooms pouring Mexican-made ales and lagers.","Range opener (spirits and craft beer), then pulque and spirits share an 'or' sentence. Now spirits and pulque together, craft beer at the end."),
'new-orleans':("New Orleans is the birthplace of classic American cocktails like the Sazerac and Vieux Carré, and its drinking culture is deeply tied to its history, with local variations of absinthe and chicory liqueurs. Visitors can explore historic and modern distilleries producing rum from Louisiana sugarcane. Craft breweries are concentrated in the Lower Garden District and Mid-City.","Distilleries and breweries share an 'or' sentence and the culture sentence comes after. Now cocktails and culture together, then distilleries, then breweries."),
'nyc':("New York City has a dense concentration of craft breweries, particularly in Brooklyn and Queens, and visitors can tour production facilities. Local spirits can be tasted at distilleries, and wine bars and dedicated tasting rooms carry a vast selection of regional and international wines.","Range opener (breweries, distilleries, wine bars), then three topics in one visit sentence. Now beer, then spirits, then wine."),
'nice-riviera':("Nice and the French Riviera are known for crisp rosés and the rare urban vineyards of the Bellet AOC. Visitors can tour estates in the hills above Nice or take day trips to the broader Côtes de Provence wine region. The harvest season in early fall provides the most active vineyard experience, while summer is prime for drinking chilled local wines on coastal terraces. The anise-flavored spirit pastis is also a regional staple.","Pastis was in the range opener with the wine. Now wine and its seasons together, pastis at the end."),
'north-island':("The North Island is a major wine destination. Hawke's Bay and Waiheke Island specialize in Syrah and Bordeaux blends, while Martinborough is known for Pinot Noir. Wellington serves as the country's craft beer hub, packed with independent breweries and taprooms.","Range opener ('wine and craft beer'). Now wine first, beer at the end."),
'paris':("Paris is a premier destination for tasting French wine, with historic cellars and dedicated tasting rooms across the city. Visitors can explore regional varieties from Bordeaux to Burgundy without leaving the capital, and the annual harvest of the city's own small vineyard in Montmartre highlights the autumn calendar. A growing craft beer movement centers around the eastern arrondissements.","Beer shared a 'while' sentence with the wine. Now wine together, beer at the end."),
'quebec-city':("Quebec's drinking culture centers on Montreal's dense craft brewery scene, with outdoor beer festivals in summer. The surrounding countryside produces specialized cider and wine, and visitors can tour the Eastern Townships' Wine Route or taste ice cider made from apples left to freeze on the branch, with fall aligned to the grape and apple harvests.","Range opener (beer, cider and wine), then the summer beer festivals come at the end beside the harvests. Now beer with its summer first, cider and wine with their fall after."),
'queenstown':("Queenstown is the gateway to the Central Otago wine region, known globally for its Pinot Noir. The Gibbston Valley, a short drive away, is packed with cellar doors and vineyards set against rugged mountains, and the best time to visit is during the warmer months when vineyard tours and outdoor tastings are most pleasant. The town also has a growing craft beer scene with local breweries and taprooms.","The warmer-months sentence came after the beer. Now it sits with the vineyards, beer last."),
'redwood':("Gateway towns around the redwoods pour local West Coast IPAs and stouts at independent breweries, and the taprooms provide a relaxed place to drink after hiking the trails. Small tasting rooms also feature regional California wines and ciders.","Range opener ('a modest craft beverage scene'), and the taprooms sentence comes after the wine. Now beer and taprooms together, wine and cider last."),
'rivieramaya':("The Riviera Maya has traditional Mexican and Mayan spirits, including xtabentún, a regional liqueur made from anise and fermented honey, and tasting rooms focus on artisanal mezcal and tequila. Craft breweries serve coastal microbrews in Playa del Carmen and Tulum.","Range opener (beer and spirits), then beer and liqueur in one 'or' sentence. Now spirits together, beer at the end."),
'uzbekistan':("Samarkand and Bukhara's local drinking culture centers on regional wines, mostly sweet and semi-sweet, often tasted at a historic winery in Samarkand. The best time to visit is during the autumn harvest, when the weather is mild and the vineyards are active. Local brandies and vodkas are also made.","Range opener, then the wine sentence mixes brandies and vodkas. Now wine and its harvest together, spirits at the end."),
'san-miguel-guanajuato':("Guanajuato's high-altitude wine route connects vineyards around San Miguel de Allende and Dolores Hidalgo, focusing on robust reds like Syrah and Cabernet Franc, and the late summer grape harvest brings the most activity to the estates. The region also produces mezcal in San Felipe and supports a growing craft brewery scene.","The harvest sentence was lumped after the mezcal and beer. Now wine and harvest together, mezcal and beer at the end."),
'santorini':("Santorini is known for its volcanic terroir, producing crisp Assyrtiko and sweet Vinsanto from basket-trained vines, and tasting rooms and vineyard tours are most active from late spring through early fall. Beyond Santorini, islands like Paros and Naxos cultivate indigenous grapes. Naxos also distills the traditional spirit Naxian Kitron.","The season sentence was lumped after the Naxos wine and spirit. Now it sits with Santorini's wine, and the spirit is split out."),
'singapore':("Singapore has a strong craft beer scene, and visitors can tour microbreweries. Local distilleries produce spirits infused with regional botanicals, including gin and rum that visitors can taste, and a cocktail scene runs alongside. Indoor taprooms and bars provide relief from the tropical heat.","Range opener (beer and cocktails, breweries and distilleries), then 'microbreweries or gin and rum' in one sentence. Now beer, then spirits."),
'sydney':("Sydney's local alcohol production centers on the Inner West, known for a dense cluster of craft breweries along the Inner West Ale Trail. Urban distilleries produce botanical gins and single malt whiskies. The nearby Hunter Valley provides classic cellar door wine tastings on day trips, and mild spring and autumn weather suits brewery hopping and vineyard walks.","Distilleries and the Hunter Valley wine share a 'while' sentence. Now beer, then spirits, then wine."),
'taiwan':("Taiwan has a long history of producing spirits, particularly Kaoliang, a strong sorghum liquor. Visitors can tour the Kavalan Distillery in Yilan County, known for whisky. Craft breweries in Taipei and Taichung add a growing beer scene, and rice and plum wines are common.","Range opener (beer and spirits), then the distillery and breweries share an 'or' sentence. Now spirits, then beer, then the rice wines last."),
'tierra-del-fuego':("Tierra del Fuego has a small but growing craft beer scene, with local breweries pouring craft beers in Ushuaia. A few distilleries use Patagonian botanicals, including gin infused with local calafate berries. The focus is on small-scale production rather than large wine regions.","Range opener (breweries and distilleries), then beer and gin in one sentence. Now beer, then gin."),
'tokyo-kyoto':("Kyoto's Fushimi district is a historic sake center lined with wooden breweries and tasting rooms along willow-draped canals. Tokyo also has historic sake production in its mountainous Okutama area, along with urban craft breweries and rooftop beer gardens.","Range opener ('brewing and distilling'), then Tokyo's sake and beer in one list. Now Kyoto's sake first, Tokyo's sake then its beer."),
'whistler':("Vancouver and Whistler are known for craft beer, with a strong brewery scene in East Vancouver. Distilleries produce gin and whisky. The nearby Fraser Valley and Vancouver Island feature wine touring, though the main Okanagan wine region is further inland, and the best time to visit is during the warmer months when brewery patios are open and regional wine tours are running.","Range opener (beer and spirits), then breweries and distilleries share a sentence. Now beer, then spirits, then wine with the season."),
'vancouver-island':("Vancouver Island has a dense craft brewery scene in Victoria. The maritime vineyards of the Cowichan Valley produce cool-climate wines like Pinot Noir and Ortega, and visitors can also tour cideries on the Saanich Peninsula. The warmest months feature full tasting room hours and vineyard patio access.","Range opener ('combines beer with vineyards'), then cider and wine share a sentence. Now beer, then wine, then cider."),
'venice':("Venice's drinking culture centers on the bacaro, traditional taverns where locals stand to drink an ombra (a small glass of Veneto wine) paired with cicchetti snacks. Visitors can taste regional Prosecco and Valpolicella while hopping between canal-side spots in Cannaregio and San Polo. The city is the birthplace of the Spritz, typically made with Aperol, Campari, or the locally preferred Select, and the peach-based Bellini.","Goes wine, then Spritz, then back to wine. Now the wine together, the Spritz and Bellini at the end."),
'vienna':("Vienna is one of the few capital cities with significant commercial vineyards within its borders. Visitors can drink the local Gemischter Satz field blend at traditional Heurigen (wine taverns) in districts like Grinzing and Nussdorf, and the scene moves from summer to the autumn wine harvests. Summer beer gardens and winter markets serving hot spiced drinks round out the year.","The last sentence ran wine, beer and winter drinks together. Now the wine together, beer gardens and winter markets at the end."),
'vietnam':("Vietnam's drinking culture centers on the daily bia hoi street corners of Hanoi, with a rapidly growing craft beer movement in Ho Chi Minh City. In the northern mountains, traditional rice and plum wines are a specialty. Dalat in the central highlands produces the country's domestic wines.","Range opener ('spans from bia hoi to craft beer'), then wines mixed in one sentence. Now beer, then rice and plum wines, then Dalat's wines."),
'snowdonia':("Wales has single malt whisky distilleries in the Brecon Beacons and North Wales. Cask ales and craft breweries operate across the country. A rising number of vineyards produce cool-climate wines in Monmouthshire and the Vale of Glamorgan, and border cider farms showcase apples.","Range opener, then ales, breweries and vineyards in one sentence. Now whisky, then beer, then wine and cider."),
'yosemite':("Just outside the park gates, the Madera Wine Trail runs south of the entrance. Inside the park, historic lodges host late-fall wine tasting events featuring California producers. The gateway towns of Mariposa and Oakhurst provide small-scale cideries and craft breweries.","Range opener ('modest local drinking scenes'). Now wine first, the cideries and breweries at the end."),
}
